{"slug":"fewest-palindrome-cuts","title":"The Fewest Cuts That Leave Only Palindromes","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":753,"tags":["dp","string","palindrome","partition"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Two tables: which pieces are palindromes, and the fewest cuts for every prefix","body":["Cut a word into pieces so that **every piece is a palindrome** (reads the same in both directions). What is the smallest number of cuts? For `aab` the answer is 1 (`aa | b`), for `abc` it is 2 (`a | b | c`), and for a word that is a palindrome itself it is 0. A word of single letters is always possible: every letter is a palindrome, so there are at most `n - 1` cuts.","First find **which pieces are palindromes**: `pal(l, r)` is true if `s[l..r]` reads the same backwards. Expand around every centre: starting from a single letter (odd length) or a pair of equal neighbours (even length), widen the piece by one letter on each side as long as the two new end letters are equal. Then let `cuts(j)` be the smallest number of cuts for the prefix ending at `j`. If the whole prefix is a palindrome, `cuts(j) = 0`; otherwise the last piece is `s[i..j]` for some `i >= 1` with `pal(i, j)`, and before it we need `cuts(i - 1)` cuts plus the cut in front of the piece: **`cuts(j) = min over i with pal(i, j) of cuts(i - 1) + 1`**.",{"code":"pal = [bytearray(n) for _ in range(n)]\nfor c in range(n):\n    for l, r in ((c, c), (c, c + 1)):          # odd and even centres\n        while l >= 0 and r < n and s[l] == s[r]:\n            pal[l][r] = 1\n            l -= 1; r += 1\ncuts = [0] * n\nfor j in range(n):\n    if pal[0][j]: cuts[j] = 0\n    else: cuts[j] = min(cuts[i - 1] + 1 for i in range(1, j + 1) if pal[i][j])\nprint(cuts[n - 1])"},"There are O(n^2) palindromic pieces and the second table looks at each once, so the whole solution is O(n^2) time and memory (about 2 million cells at the limit). Splitting a problem into \"precompute a yes/no table\" and \"optimise over the allowed pieces\" is the common shape of partition problems."]},"statement":["A word `s` is given. Cut it (between letters) into pieces so that each piece is a palindrome. Print the smallest possible number of cuts."],"inputFormat":["One line with the word `s`."],"outputFormat":["Print the smallest number of cuts."],"constraints":["1 <= length of s <= 1500","The word consists of lowercase English letters."],"examples":[{"input":"aab\n","output":"1\n","note":"aa | b: 1 cut."},{"input":"abc\n","output":"2\n","note":"a | b | c: 2 cuts."}],"hints":["First mark all palindromic pieces by expanding around every centre.","Let cuts(j) be the answer for the prefix ending at j: 0 if it is a palindrome, otherwise the best over the last palindromic piece s[i..j].","Remember the extra cut in front of the last piece."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["All palindromic pieces are marked by expanding around every centre; cuts(j), the fewest cuts for the prefix ending at j, is 0 if the prefix is a palindrome and otherwise the smallest cuts(i - 1) + 1 over the palindromic pieces s[i..j]. The answer is cuts(n - 1)."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2), space O(n^2).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\n\nn = len(s)\npal = [bytearray(n) for _ in range(n)]\nfor c in range(n):\n    l = r = c\n    while l >= 0 and r < n and s[l] == s[r]:\n        pal[l][r] = 1\n        l -= 1\n        r += 1\n    l, r = c, c + 1\n    while l >= 0 and r < n and s[l] == s[r]:\n        pal[l][r] = 1\n        l -= 1\n        r += 1\ncuts = [0] * n\nfor j in range(n):\n    if pal[0][j]:\n        cuts[j] = 0\n    else:\n        best = j\n        for i in range(1, j + 1):\n            if pal[i][j] and cuts[i - 1] + 1 < best:\n                best = cuts[i - 1] + 1\n        cuts[j] = best\nprint(cuts[n - 1])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    int n = (int)s.size();\n    vector<vector<char>> pal(n, vector<char>(n, 0));\n    for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n        int l = c, r = c;\n        while (l >= 0 && r < n && s[l] == s[r]) { pal[l][r] = 1; l--; r++; }\n        l = c; r = c + 1;\n        while (l >= 0 && r < n && s[l] == s[r]) { pal[l][r] = 1; l--; r++; }\n    }\n    vector<int> cuts(n, 0);\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n        if (pal[0][j]) { cuts[j] = 0; continue; }\n        int best = j;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= j; i++) {\n            if (pal[i][j] && cuts[i - 1] + 1 < best) best = cuts[i - 1] + 1;\n        }\n        cuts[j] = best;\n    }\n    cout << cuts[n - 1] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n\n        int n = s.length();\n        boolean[][] pal = new boolean[n][n];\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n            int l = c, r = c;\n            while (l >= 0 && r < n && s.charAt(l) == s.charAt(r)) { pal[l][r] = true; l--; r++; }\n            l = c; r = c + 1;\n            while (l >= 0 && r < n && s.charAt(l) == s.charAt(r)) { pal[l][r] = true; l--; r++; }\n        }\n        int[] cuts = new int[n];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            if (pal[0][j]) { cuts[j] = 0; continue; }\n            int best = j;\n            for (int i = 1; i <= j; i++) {\n                if (pal[i][j] && cuts[i - 1] + 1 < best) best = cuts[i - 1] + 1;\n            }\n            cuts[j] = best;\n        }\n        System.out.println(cuts[n - 1]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"aab\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"abc\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"a\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"aa\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"abba\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"abcba\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"aabaababababaaaaaabb\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"cacccbbcaacbacbbaabcabaabbbcbbabbbaacccabbabcaacaabcccabbbcbcbacacabaaacbbbaaaababbcacacabbabcaccacc\n","output":"34\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"204\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"138\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"1345\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"225\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"457\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"1481\n"}]}